# Testing strategy

## Pyramid

| Level | Share | Dependencies |
| ----------- | ----- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Unit | Most | All external I/O mocked |
| Integration | Some | Real DB or sandbox; mock third parties |
| E2E | Least | Full path; mock only uncontrollable externals |

## Decision tree

```
External integration contract? → Integration tests
Pure business logic? → Unit tests
Full user journey? → E2E
UI component? → Component tests + API mocks
Database touched? → Factories + isolated cleanup per test run
```

## Conventions

- Name: `should <outcome> when <condition>`
- Structure: Arrange → Act → Assert
- Multi-tenant / multi-user: unique isolated fixture per run; tear down in `afterAll`
- Invariant-linked tests: name after behavior (`should_refund_idempotently`) — **⊥** `TestV7_*` / `§V` in product test names

## E2E essentials

- Test user behavior, not implementation
- Stable selectors: `data-testid`, roles, labels — not CSS classes or `nth-child`
- Independent tests; deterministic; proper waits (not fixed sleeps)
- Page objects for shared navigation; clean up test data per run
- Mock external APIs when possible; parallelize in CI

